// codebox_enc.gen -- f_formconstants render stage: the inverse retinotopic
// resample. Maps each output pixel's visual-field polar coords (r, theta) to
// cortical (u, v) = (k_ecc*log(1 + sqrt(r^2 + r_soft^2)/r0), k_ang*theta) and
// samples the E field there, periodic in both cortical axes.
// Runs at render resolution AND SO DOES THE STATE (FR-001: solver res ==
// render res; `r dim` resizes every stage) -- no reconstruction filter is
// needed or wanted: hardware-exact manual bilinear WITH WRAP, mirroring
// tests/modules/formconstants/fc_mirror.encode() term for term (the f_wc
// 16-tap Catmull-Rom exists to hide 256^2-quantized contours, the artifact
// class this module does not have -- tasks.md record 2026-10-24).
// Mirror: tests/modules/formconstants/fc_mirror.encode().
//
// Inputs: in1 = the `r draw` bang (not referenced here), in2 = the state
// (R = E, from the nl stage).
//   - the cortical sample: fx = cv*sw - 0.5, fy = cu*sh - 0.5, floor +
//     fractions, 4 nearest texel-centre reads wrapped per axis, lerp. The
//     state size comes from the sw/sh PARAMS (raw `r dim` -> route/unpack ->
//     prepend param), NOT the `dim` global: `dim` is not an input texture's
//     size (jit-gen-codebox skill: manual taps need the size as a literal or
//     a Param; the 2026-10-24 solid-flicker debug found enc/seed's in1
//     bound-texture dims degenerate)
//   - the cortical axes: u (eccentricity) = ROWS, v (angle) = COLUMNS (the
//     f_wc mirror convention, retained so the map records/render scripts
//     compare directly)
//   - map constants are dials (defaults from G0's stills: zoom 5, twist 3,
//     fovea 1.0 -- the CLOSER set, the best read at the fine web scale;
//     retune Phase 2); r_max 4 stays baked (the f_wc field of view)
//   - FOVEAL SOFTENING (f_wc 2026-10-24, retained): u flattens for
//     r << r_soft so the log-singularity vortex becomes a calm disc;
//     r_soft is a bench-vary Param
//   - display mapping (f_wc G4): E is already a 0..1 rate; contrast stretch
//     about mid-gray, then sharp blends toward the crisp S-curve; default
//     0.5 (f_wc's soak finding)
//   - non-finite E maps to 0 (abs(x) < 1e30 guard: NaN == NaN is TRUE here)
//   - bypass_gate = 1 outputs black with alpha 1 (the f_chladni generator
//     convention); the solver keeps running upstream. The Param is never
//     named `bypass` (native pix attribute, f_wc FR-010's lesson)
Param bypass_gate(0);
Param sharp(0.5);
Param contrast(1.0);
Param k_ecc(5.0);
Param k_ang(3);
Param r0(1.0);
Param r_soft(0.35);
Param sw(128);
Param sh(128);

px = (norm.x * 2 - 1) * 4;
py = (norm.y * 2 - 1) * 4;
r, theta = cartopol(px, py);
u = k_ecc * log(1 + sqrt(r * r + r_soft * r_soft) / r0);
v = k_ang * theta;
cu = fract(u / twopi);
cv = fract(v / twopi);

fx = cv * sw - 0.5;
fy = cu * sh - 0.5;
x0 = floor(fx);
y0 = floor(fy);
tx = fx - x0;
ty = fy - y0;
xa0 = x0 - sw * floor(x0 / sw);
xb0 = (x0 + 1) - sw * floor((x0 + 1) / sw);
ya0 = y0 - sh * floor(y0 / sh);
yb0 = (y0 + 1) - sh * floor((y0 + 1) / sh);
cxa = (xa0 + 0.5) / sw;
cxb = (xb0 + 0.5) / sw;
cya = (ya0 + 0.5) / sh;
cyb = (yb0 + 0.5) / sh;
e00 = nearest(in2, vec(cxa, cya)).x;
e10 = nearest(in2, vec(cxb, cya)).x;
e01 = nearest(in2, vec(cxa, cyb)).x;
e11 = nearest(in2, vec(cxb, cyb)).x;
au = (1 - ty) * ((1 - tx) * e00 + tx * e10) + ty * ((1 - tx) * e01 + tx * e11);

au = switch(abs(au) < 1e30, au, 0);
soft = clamp((clamp(au, 0, 1) - 0.5) * contrast + 0.5, 0, 1);
crisp = smoothstep(0.46, 0.54, soft);
lum = mix(soft, crisp, sharp);
lum = lum * (1 - bypass_gate);

out1 = vec(lum, lum, lum, 1);
